WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.000
-Our next guest
is a talented actress

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.367
who stars in the new romantic
comedy "I Want You Back,"

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:08.133
which premieres February 11th
on Prime Video.

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.634
Please welcome Jenny Slate!

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:12.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:15.834
Oh, my bud! Oh, my buddy!

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:18.267
So good to see you, Jenny.
Jenny Slate.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:19.367
-Hi, Jimmy. Hi.

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:21.701
-Jenny,
I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:24.067
I just wanted to say
congratulations.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.234
You're married. You have a baby.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:28.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:32.701
How is the baby?
How is it all going?

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:34.868
-It's going -- I think - I mean,
you will have to ask her,

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.734
although she can't talk yet,

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:40.133
but I think it's going well just
in terms of how we're vibing,

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:41.400
I feel like.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.067
-What is she into now?

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:45.567
What's the new thing?

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.667
-What she's into now is jokes.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:51.167
She likes --
She likes my comedy, but --

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:53.400
I know. My comedy
has become comedy for babies.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.801
Like, the hit around this house
is I take her pacifier.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:00.501
I just did it, by the way,
for my friends.

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:03.734
I go, "Can I try this?"
And she's like, "Eh."

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:06.334
And I'm like,
"Is it spicy? Is it spicy?"

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:07.801
And she's like, "Eh."

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:10.634
And then I put it in my mouth,
and I'm like -- [ Groans ]

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:12.200
And then I kind of,
like, spit it out,

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.834
and that's apparently
the best work I've ever done.

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:18.133
-[ Laughter ]
-That's a good bit.

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:19.601
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:22.234
-I want to talk about
your wedding because,

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:23.634
again, congratulations.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:27.734
But I know it was pushed a bunch
of times because of the pandemic

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:28.901
and then you were just like,

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:30.567
"You know what?
We're going to do it.

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:31.801
I don't care. We're doing it."

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:34.167
You got married in your home.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:36.467
-We got married
on New Year's Eve

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:39.400
after four other times
of trying to get married.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.901
We got married
in the living room.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.467
And there were 23 people.

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:48.033
It was -- It was a small affair.

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:50.501
We weren't -- Like it or not,
we weren't able to get a refund

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:52.634
on a lot of the things
that we booked

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.601
when we thought we were
going to have like 200 people.

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:56.968
So we had the flowers
that you would have

00:01:56.968 --> 00:01:59.901
for like a 200-person wedding
but for 23 people.

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:02.234
So it was very decadent,
I think, yeah.

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:03.601
-You brought us a photo,
which --

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:05.767
Thank you very much
for doing this.

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.100
Look at you guys here.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.701
How cute is that? Come on.

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:09.834
[ Audience awws ]

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:12.167
That is just -- Come on.

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:14.601
And was the baby --

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:17.534
Did the baby partake
in the wedding at all?

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:19.801
Was she part of the wedding?

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:22.734
-You know, it was
a tight guest list, as I said.

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:23.968
-[ Laughter ]
-Wow!

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:25.868
Wow!
You didn't even invite the baby.

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:28.334
Alright. Understood.
Yeah, I mean, hey --

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.601
That's another plate
right there, yeah.

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:33.133
-Just like, you know,
"I just met you.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:35.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:39.601
We got married
in between snack time

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:44.501
and dinnertime for the baby,
and so she was there.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.033
And then -- And we got married,

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:48.334
and, like,
it was just very few people,

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.501
but I still wore
a beautiful gown.

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:52.968
Like, kind of
one of the fanciest things

00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:56.133
I've ever worn in my life
to make, you know,

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:58.734
like, the walk up "the aisle"
from my bedroom

00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:00.434
to the corner
of the living room.

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:02.634
-Yeah.
-But, like, after a while,

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:05.400
it was time to put the baby
to sleep, and so, like,

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.767
I left the wedding in my gown
to put the baby to bed,

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:11.834
like, gave her the bottle
and put her to bed.

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:13.667
Like, if any parents
are out there,

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:16.567
you know that once the baby
is asleep you are just like,

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:19.634
"Please don't --
Just please stay asleep

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:21.734
for just a little bit,
just a little bit."

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.701
-Yeah.
-And on my wedding night --

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:25.634
Again,
I wouldn't have imagined this.

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:30.133
I crawled on my hands and knees
out of the baby's room,

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:33.567
like, in my very fancy dress.

00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:35.267
-"Everyone be quiet."
-And as I passed by --

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:37.834
And someone was being loud
in the bedroom next door.

00:03:37.834 --> 00:03:39.634
My friend's kids
were watching "The Hobbit."

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:42.067
And I, like, opened the door
still on my hands and knees

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:43.901
and was like,
"Turn 'The Hobbit' down!"

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:47.734
And I was just like --
On my wedding night,

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:49.868
you know, I don't think I would
have imagined just yelling

00:03:49.868 --> 00:03:51.100
"Turn 'The Hobbit' down."

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.767
-Yeah. Oh, yeah.
That's interesting.

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:56.567
You can't predict this stuff.
-You can't.

00:03:56.567 --> 00:03:58.467
You just --
You just got to stay romantic.

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:00.467
-Yeah.
-And stay hopeful.

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:01.968
-How about that for a segue?

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:05.133
Let's talk about your romantic
comedy called "I Want You Back."

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:08.634
It's you and Charlie Day,
who is unbelievably funny.

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:10.767
What a great dude.
He is so funny.

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:12.467
-What a gentleman. Yeah.

00:04:12.467 --> 00:04:14.467
-You guys have great chemistry.
Have you worked together?

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:16.033
-I think we do.
-Have you done stuff together?

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:18.534
-Thank you for saying so.
Yeah, he's a real class act.

00:04:18.534 --> 00:04:20.534
I met him before we shot.

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:23.334
But right before we -- Ten weeks
before we made the movie,

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:25.234
I had my daughter.

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:28.701
So I met him and I was like
nine months pregnant,

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:31.067
wearing these, like, gigantic
overalls, and I was like,

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:34.000
"You'll be falling in love
with me, you know."

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:40.267
"I'm the girl of your dreams.
I'm super pregnant."

00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:42.601
And then I really
got to know him on set,

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:45.133
and he truly is, like,
such a class act.

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:50.767
He's a comedy star,
but also just what a darling.

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:53.501
-Can we set up the movie at all?
-Sure.

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:55.100
Yeah.
Sure, I know what it is about.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.200
I was in it. Yeah.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.634
-Yeah.
-I play a character named Emma.

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:00.300
Charlie plays Peter.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:03.501
We have both been dumped
at the beginning of the movie.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:07.434
And we meet while we are crying
in a stairwell, separately.

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:09.601
And then we notice
each other crying,

00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:14.667
and then we decide to support
each other through our sadness,

00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:16.868
and that quickly turns
into hatching a scheme

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:19.901
to try to get our exes back
for each other.

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:21.167
-I want to show a clip.

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:23.133
Here's Jenny Slate
in "I Want You Back."

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:24.667
Take a look at this.

00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:27.934
-What about this?
It's a good plan. Hear me out.

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:29.801
-Mm-hmm.
-How about whenever

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:32.100
we are feeling like
we really have to call them

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.601
and we just can't
take it anymore...

00:05:33.601 --> 00:05:34.934
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:37.868
-Instead of calling our exes,
let's call each other.

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:40.200
-Hmm! I love that!
-Yeah?

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.067
-I love it because we're
intercepting each other's heads.

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:44.334
-Yes.

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:46.501
-Yes! We're each other
sadness sisters.

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:49.367
-Well, "sadness sisters" sounds
like you're Diane Keaton

00:05:49.367 --> 00:05:51.667
and I'm Meryl Streep
and we're in a Broadway play,

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:53.033
but I like it, yeah.

00:05:53.033 --> 00:05:56.367
-That's a great cast.
You should cast plays.

00:05:56.367 --> 00:06:00.601
-Yeah, you should cast plays.
Jenny Slate, everybody.

00:06:00.601 --> 00:06:04.000
"I Want You Back" premieres
February 11th on Prime Video.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.634
So happy for you, bud.

